<tool id="neutrons_radar_pd_live_snapshot_prototype" name="RADAR-PD Utility: Live Snapshot Analysis" version="0.1.10" profile="22.05">
    <description>analyze one immutable provisional scan against a reviewed nuclear reference</description>
    <requirements><container type="docker">@IMMUTABLE_MODELS_IMAGE@</container></requirements>
    <command detect_errors="exit_code"><![CDATA[
        touch '$result_bundle' '$response_cache_output' '$console_output' &&
        trap "chmod a+r '$result_bundle' '$response_cache_output' '$console_output' >/dev/null 2>&1 || true" EXIT &&
        python -m gpx_recipe.live.galaxy_worker '$packet' worker '$result_bundle' '$response_cache_output' --preparation-evidence '$preparation_provenance' #slurp
        #if $response_cache
            --cache '$response_cache' #slurp
        #end if
        > '$console_output' 2>&1
    ]]></command>
    <configfiles>
@PREPARATION_PROVENANCE@
    </configfiles>
    <inputs>
        <param name="packet" type="data" format="zip" label="Reviewed source, observations and magnetic settings"/>
        <param name="response_cache" type="data" format="zip" optional="true" label="Compatible native response cache"/>
        <param name="preparation_evidence" type="data" format="json" multiple="true" optional="true" label="Native preparation origin receipts (NOVA supplies these automatically)"/>
        <param name="dispatch_key" type="text" label="NOVA dispatch identity">
            <validator type="regex" message="Use the NOVA-generated dispatch key">^[a-f0-9]{24}$</validator>
        </param>
    </inputs>
    <outputs>
        <data name="result_bundle" format="zip" label="RADAR-PD live snapshot result bundle"/>
        <data name="response_cache_output" format="zip" label="RADAR-PD live snapshot response cache"/>
        <data name="console_output" format="txt" label="RADAR-PD live snapshot console"/>
        <collection name="verified_projects" type="list" label="Verified conditional live-snapshot GPXs">
            <discover_datasets pattern="(?P&lt;designation>.+)\.gpx" ext="binary" directory="worker/verified_projects" visible="true"/>
        </collection>
    </outputs>
    <help><![CDATA[
NOVA captures and reviews the provisional scan and nuclear reference before
submitting this worker. Cumulative snapshots replace the likelihood; they are
not added to one another. Cache reuse requires matching observations geometry,
fixed reference, magnetic settings and scientific implementation.

The result reports conditional uncertainty and sampling diagnostics. It does
not establish a phase, calibrated stopping decision or a converged conventional
Rietveld refinement. Published GPXs represent the verified displayed parameter
values; the original source is preserved. No model API credential is required.

Prepared model inputs use the same creating-job evidence contract as Model
Campaign. A receipt alone does not qualify another geometry, bank or data set.
    ]]></help>
</tool>
